  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion provides meaningful value over unimodal approaches, and what a strong 'standard' multimodal configuration achieves. config_004 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion) is the most informative first experiment because: (1) it directly tests the core hypothesis of the study—whether combining RNA and image modalities helps—using strong, well-motivated defaults for each component (learned scVI embedding for RNA, pre-trained ViT-L for images); (2) by choosing singleprofile and weighted fusion, it keeps the design simple and interpretable, so any future degradation can be attributed to specific design choices rather than compounding complexity; (3) it establishes a performance reference point that will anchor all subsequent comparisons (multiprofile, alternative encoders, transformer aggregation, concat fusion, unimodal baselines). Starting here avoids the risk of a complex configuration failing for ambiguous reasons, and the result will efficiently guide whether to explore multiprofile/aggregation next or to test unimodal baselines to quantify the multimodal gain."
}

